		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagSession"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " owns the radio \u2013 "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagCodec"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " owns the bytes, and neither reaches across. Passing a payload between them is seamless because both sides already speak "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagRecord"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", so the codec can be tested with no device attached."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "If the tag leaves the field before the read finishes, CoreNFC calls back with a user-cancelled invalidation or, more often, a timeout. Both map to one message on screen: \"Tag was moved away too quickly. Hold it against the top of the phone until the tick appears.\" The mapping table lives in "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagError+Message.swift"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", and the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"kind": "internal",
					"slug": "reference/api",
					"anchor": "errors",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Tag session API"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " lists every case."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "ChipProfiles"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " ships the public capability table in the App Store build. Our internal builds add station-pack-alpha, the profile set for the reader hardware on the test bench, through a separate package target that the release scheme excludes."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Contoso Tap keeps its codec inside the app target, which is a reasonable choice if there is never going to be a command line tool. We split ours out in 1.1.0 and got the fuzz tests for free."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"id": "what-was-removed",
			"idSource": "slug",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "What was removed"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "strikethrough",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "SyncEngine"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " came out in 1.1.0. It mirrored scan history to a server account, and it was the only package that opened a network connection. Removing it dropped the network entitlement and about four hundred lines of migration code. Scan history is local now, and the export button in Settings writes a JSON file."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The name still appears in the 1.0 tag. Do not revive it for something smaller, because the entitlement comes back with it."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"id": "adding-a-package",
			"idSource": "slug",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Adding a package"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "New code goes in an existing package unless it needs a dependency that package cannot take. When it does need one, place the package in the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"kind": "anchor",
					"anchor": "module-graph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "module graph"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " before writing any code, because its position decides what it is allowed to import."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"style": "ordered",
			"tight": true,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Create it with "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "swift package init --type library"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Add it to "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "Fixture.xcworkspace"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " and to the app target."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Add a row to "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "Docs/module-graph.txt"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": ", the source of the tree above."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Run "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "make graph-check"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " and fix whatever it names."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "callout",
			"kind": "note",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "make graph-check"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " reads every "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "import"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " statement under "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "Packages/*/Sources"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " and fails on an upward edge. A package that imports "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "AppShell"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " will not reach review."
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"title": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Import direction is checked"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
